s a big  difference sure but the the general  point is that it scales based on the  number of streams and the  characteristics of the stream so to give  an example just if you had just have  three HD 1080p streams at 30 frames per  second you can use a tiny little box  that will handle those three and then if  you go to six you can just linearly  stack more boxes okay but you can also  run box as a virtual machine on any set  of servers so if you have a hundred and  twenty cameras on campus you can run  that on a  single-server if it's beefy enough  understand so we have tools that  estimate you you enter in the  characteristics of your stream like I  have 1080p streams at 30 frames per  second at this four megabit encoding  rate and then it spits out your  recommended number of boxes based on the  number of CPUs and number of memory and  stuff so I hate to say it depends but it  really does depend we're trying to make  it simple by using a spreadsheet that is  on our site that will give you an answer  to this question is a help article on  how do i scale to the number of streams  that I'm monitoring fantastic all right  that's all the questions we had Carter  thank you so much for being here really  appreciated folks on on the stream thank  you so much for tuning in we sincerely  hope you have found this useful and  informative I think was a great way to  kind of showcase some of the really cool  capabilities of GCP things like auto  scaling and the ability to kind of  ingest these massive amounts of data and  do some machine learning processing on  them before we sign off I want to let  you know that if you've enjoyed this  format you should tune in to a more  formal sorry a less formal session that  we run once or twice a week it's called  the GCP online Meetup you can find us on  meetup.com or subscribe to us on youtube  at youtube.com slash GCP live we'll be  signing off but please stay tuned for  the next session called accelerating  your google cloud migration which should  be coming to you live from the Google  New York office shortly thank you and  have a great day  you

